content:
This sample policy moves an index from hot storage to UltraWarm, and eventually to
cold storage. Then, it deletes the index.
The index is initially in the hot state. After ten days, ISM moves it
to the warm state. 80 days later, after the index is 90 days old, ISM moves the index to the
cold state. After a year, the service sends a notiﬁcation to an Amazon Chime room that the index
is being deleted and then permanently deletes it.
Note that cold indexes require the cold_delete operation rather than the normal delete
operation. Also note that an explicit timestamp_field is required in your data in order to
manage cold indexes with ISM.
{
"policy": {
"description": "Demonstrate a hot-warm-cold-delete workflow.",
